Scope

The license above (0BSD) covers only this fork's own work:

- the files the fork adds: arm64/, .github/workflows/arm64.yml,
  .github/workflows/arm64-fft-harness.yml,
  .github/workflows/arm64-lavapipe-harness.yml,
  .github/workflows/arm64-guard.yml, README.md and this LICENSE;
- the fork's own additions to .github/workflows/arm64-gate.yml and
  tools/engine.py;
- the fork's own lines in the patches under arm64/patches/ that change
  upstream's scripts.

It does not cover anything else:

- A patch hunk to a third-party file keeps that file's license: MPL-2.0 for
  Mozilla files, BSD-3-Clause for Skia (gfx/skia), LGPL-2.1-or-later for ffvpx
  (media/ffvpx, including the new tx_float_x86eq.c, a port of ffvpx code) and
  MIT for Mesa (the lavapipe patch).
- Upstream's own files (oss-invisible/firefox_antidetect_patch), and the parts
  of the fork's workflows copied from them, are not relicensed. They stay
  under whatever terms upstream gives them.
